      "reasoning": "All three answers agree with the earlier answers and their own captured worked solutions. q-73495: interval I contains a jump at zero because the left and right limits are −1 and 1; II is closed and the exponential branch is continuous throughout it; III is not closed. Thus only II satisfies the extreme value theorem's hypotheses. q-131066: I contains a jump at zero with one-sided limits 2 and 0; II is closed and tangent is continuous there; III includes π/2, where tangent is undefined. Thus only II qualifies. q-104148: the left limit is (3+3)/3=2 and the right limit is 12/(3+3)=2, so the two-sided limit exists and equals 2, whereas f(−√3)=3. The discontinuity is therefore caused by the limit differing from the function value. No grades were supplied; the MA evidence comes from the captured worked solutions.",
